And they do that, again, geographically separated at different places because it represents something. It stirs up something in them. It's about resistance. It's about, let's say, freedom. It's about rebellion and also energy. So this is then expressed in this flag. So someone came up with this story, created then all this imagery, and it speaks to people.

00:10:48.621 --> 00:11:31.702
So people pick it up and then use it in their own life, for example, when they try to overthrow their government. Similarly to the American flag, which also pops up quite often, for example, in the protests in Hong Kong. So there are certain images and certain emotions that are then intertwined. And Jung talks about that, that he says Archetypes are full of energy.

00:11:32.411 --> 00:11:56.274
They're human forms of life, have a tremendous attraction, and they grip one again and again if one doesn't look out. So an archetype does something with us. So it is in us, it does something with us, and we also experience it outside. And he says archetypes have one really, really big advantage. They are not random.

00:11:56.514 --> 00:12:21.001
They are within us. They are in the collective part of our psyche. He has a very evolutionary approach. He says there are certain situations, uh, that happened so often in the past that they became kind of ingrained in us. So when human beings are born, we are not empty. We already have these images, these patterns of behavior, these emotions within us.

00:12:21.354 --> 00:12:37.765
Every human being that is born has it, and then it expresses itself through that human being. And he says the very, very big advantage is that certain things happened so often in the past that we are kind of smarter than we know.

00:12:40.061 --> 00:13:03.215
It means that we in our consciousness, what we know, how we would describe ourselves to another person, like, this is my name, this is my age, these are the things. I've been done and these are things I want to do. He says there's a more complete psyche below that that can be activated in the right situation. And these, this is what these quotes are about.

00:13:04.830 --> 00:13:28.708
They serve as an essential safeguard against situations in which one might lose one's composure. Whenever a panic situation arises, whether external or internal, the archetypes step in and help a person react in an instinctively appropriate way, as if they had always known the situation. They react the way humanity has always reacted.

00:13:29.302 --> 00:13:49.596
That is why this mechanism is vital. Meaning we have the archetype of the hero because people acted heroically in the past. We have the archetype of a relationship because people got into relationships in the past. We have the archetypes of mother or father because people had mothers and fathers also in the past.

00:13:49.676 --> 00:14:12.122
So there's already an understanding, like a repertoire, a toolbox of behavior available to us, not necessarily actively, but it comes out at the right situations when it is needed. In the movie Cast Away, where he gets stranded on an island and has to survive, and we kind of have that still in us that we find a way how to survive in nature.

00:14:14.601 --> 00:14:37.863
