00:14:38.428 --> 00:15:00.384
For since eternity, man has gone through situations with which he could not cope, where instincts had to step in and solve the situations, either in a cunning way or by a coup de force. Interestingly enough, Tom Hanks played in another movie called Sully, where he plays this pilot that saved the plane that crashed into the Hudson River in New York.

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:21.876
And It was an absolutely crazy maneuver he did, and it worked out because he was highly, highly capable, but he also kept his calm because they got something activated inside of him. That's based on a, on a real story. And you have that very often that people rise to the occasion under certain circumstances and become then heroes.

00:15:21.925 --> 00:15:45.650
And these are the people we like to hear about and we tell stories about. So Jung sees there really an underlying pattern. It's not that we are talking about one hero or one relationship or one king that died, but rather it's a more like general pattern that is abstractly described. And it has a lot of expressions.

00:15:45.698 --> 00:16:05.104
It has a lot of different facets. So this is why there's this book of Joseph Campbell with the name Hero with a Thousand Faces. Like Luke Skywalker is a hero, Harry Potter is a hero, Neo is a hero. And they all have something in common, a common core. And Jung would describe that as then the heroic archetype.

00:16:05.972 --> 00:16:28.702
